1156:
In addition, the board of commissioners shall consider, at a minimum, the following in its determination of whether or not to zone property to limited use historic:
(1) Whether or not quiet enjoyment of surrounding property will be adversely affected;
(2) Whether or not adequate provisions are made for waste disposal, parking and traffic;
(3) Whether or not the intensity of the use is appropriate in light of the surrounding land uses and the historical nature of the property;
(4) Whether adequate provisions are made to maintain the historical authenticity and integrity of the property; and
(5) Whether the times and hours of operation will adversely effect the use of the adjoining properties.
